{"question": "What role do internal compartments and membranes play in maintaining the organization of the human body?", "type": "factual", "provenance": "llm_drafted_human_verified", "reference": "Internal compartments keep body cells separated from external environmental threats while keeping them moist and nourished. They also separate internal body fluids from microorganisms on body surfaces, such as those in the intestinal tract.", "gold_chunk_ids": ["anatomy-and-physiology-p0024-00"], "gold_pages": ["Anatomy and Physiology, 1.3. Functions of Human Life*, p.14"], "books": ["anatomy-and-physiology"], "notes": "NEEDS REVIEW: verify the passage answers this and that retrieval is required.", "id": "fact-003"}
