{"question": "How does a hyperbaric chamber treat decompression sickness (DCS)?", "type": "factual", "provenance": "llm_drafted_human_verified", "reference": "A hyperbaric chamber treats DCS by repressurizing the body so that pressure can be removed much more gradually. It also introduces oxygen at high pressure, which increases oxygen concentration in the blood and replaces some of the nitrogen with oxygen that is easier to tolerate out of solution.", "gold_chunk_ids": ["anatomy-and-physiology-p0030-01"], "gold_pages": ["Anatomy and Physiology, 1.5. Homeostasis*, p.20"], "books": ["anatomy-and-physiology"], "notes": "NEEDS REVIEW: verify the passage answers this and that retrieval is required.", "id": "fact-005"}
