{"question": "What effect does parathyroid hormone (PTH) have on osteoclast proliferation and activity?", "type": "factual", "provenance": "llm_drafted_human_verified", "reference": "Parathyroid hormone (PTH) stimulates osteoclast proliferation and activity. As a result, calcium is released from the bones into the circulation, increasing the calcium ion concentration in the blood.", "gold_chunk_ids": ["anatomy-and-physiology-p0255-00"], "gold_pages": ["Anatomy and Physiology, 6.7. Calcium Homeostasis: Interactions of the Skeletal System and Other Organ Systems*, p.245"], "books": ["anatomy-and-physiology"], "notes": "NEEDS REVIEW: verify the passage answers this and that retrieval is required.", "id": "fact-022"}
{"question": "What physical form does uric acid tend to take when excreted by animals such as birds, insects, and reptiles?", "type": "factual", "provenance": "llm_drafted_human_verified", "reference": "Uric acid is water insoluble and tends to form a white paste or powder when excreted by birds, insects, and reptiles.", "gold_chunk_ids": ["biology-p1215-02"], "gold_pages": ["Biology, 41.4. Nitrogenous Wastes*, p.1203"], "books": ["biology"], "notes": "NEEDS REVIEW: verify the passage answers this and that retrieval is required.", "id": "fact-023"}
